    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just gone. everything i used to be able to write, everything that made me feel alive... it's just empty now. i look at the sheet music and it's like i'm looking at a stranger's handwriting. i feel like i've hit a wall that's literally impossible to climb over. it's not just a slump, it feels like the end of the road.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you are experiencing a profound creative block, which can feel incredibly isolating and defeating. Please know that this feeling, while intense, is a very common part of the creative process, even for the most experienced artists. Try setting aside the pressure to create something \"good\" for a while and just engage with music in a purely receptive way. Sometimes, stepping away from the goal and simply listening or exploring sounds can help unlock new pathways.",
